cartridge "MOON LANDING/C. KOSNIOWSKI/1983"

' MOON LANDING - ColecoVision version of the Oric game by Czes Kosniowski
' ("Games to Play on Your Oric-1", Shiva 1983, game 3). Adapted by Amy &
' Claude, Amy Studio 2026. Built by build.py from this file,
' ../_common/amy/core.alexis, pages.txt, art.py and music/*.txt.
'
' THE GAME (as in the book): a lunar module in free fall. Each moment the
' speed grows (gravity) and the height drops by the speed; the retro rocket
' (here: a button) brakes and burns fuel. Three bar gauges with 1/8-cell
' resolution show VELOCITY, HEIGHT and FUEL. Touchdown speed: 10 or less
' WELL DONE, 11-20 NOT BAD, 21-100 CRASH LANDING; over 100 at any time the
' module explodes. Start: height 1990, speed 10, full tank.
'
' CONTROLS: a button fires the retro rocket while held. Joystick left/right
' fires the side jets (a little fuel). Title: up/down choose, left/right
' change the starting level, a button confirms.
'
' LIBERTIES (listed for Amy):
' - A visible module (sprites, thrust flame, side-jet puffs) comes down
'   onto a moonscape with a landing pad; the book only had the gauges.
'   Landing off the pad is a crash ("MISSED THE PAD").
' - Levels: gravity, fuel burn and wind grow, the module starts off the pad
'   from level 2 (table for levels 1-8, then the last values; tuned with
'   model/moonsim.py, checked with tests/bot.mjs). Level 1 is the book's
'   game, a little kinder (gravity 80 %, burn at the book's minimum).
' - WELL DONE and NOT BAD land you (next level); a crash costs one of three
'   lives (the book had one go and "Another go? Y or N").
' - The speed never goes below 0 (the book let the module climb).
' - Speed zones are coloured on the VELOCITY gauge: green to 10, yellow to
'   20, red above, magenta 90-100; FUEL turns yellow below 1/4, red below 1/10.
' - The engine noise follows the speed (the book's SOUND 4,125-V/4) and is
'   louder while the rocket burns; it is written straight to the PSG after
'   each frame's NMI (sub Engine). Music and the other effects are new; the
'   Oric's PING and EXPLODE are kept as cues.

